"doi":"10.1038/s41467-019-12990-0","metadata":{"abstract":"Transcript assembly from RNA-seq reads is a critical step in gene expression and subsequent functional analyses. Here we present PsiCLASS, an accurate and efficient transcript assembler based on an approach that simultaneously analyzes multiple RNA-seq samples. PsiCLASS combines mixture statistical models for exonic feature selection across multiple samples with splice graph based dynamic programming algorithms and a weighted voting scheme for transcript selection. PsiCLASS achieves significantly better sensitivity-precision tradeoff, and renders precision up to 2-3 fold higher than the StringTie system and Scallop plus TACO, the two best current approaches. PsiCLASS is efficient and scalable, assembling 667 GEUVADIS samples in 9 h, and has robust accuracy with large numbers of samples.","authors":[{"name":"Florea L."},{"name":"Sabunciyan S."},{"name":"Song L."},{"name":"Yang G."}],"citationCount":25,"date":"2019-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Communications","title":"A multi-sample approach increases the accuracy of transcript assembly"},"pmcid":"PMC6825223","pmid":"31676772"}],"topic":[{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"PsiCLASS","home":"https://bio.tools/psiclass","license":"GPL-1.0","summary":"Reference-based transcriptome assembler for single or multiple RNA-seq samples","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"1.0.3","first_commit":"2023-09-06","conda_name":"psiclass","conda_version":"1.0.3","summary":"PsiCLASS is a reference-based transcriptome assembler for single or multiple RNA-seq samples.","edam_operations":["Transcriptome assembly"],"edam_topics":["Sequence assembly"],"toolshed_categories":["Transcriptomics"],"toolshed_id":"psiclass","users_5_years":11,"users_all_time":11,"usage_5_years":46,"usage_all_time":46,"bio_tools_summary":"Reference-based transcriptome assembler for single or multiple RNA-seq samples","bio